{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/812198-htr-changing-perceptions-on-the-wod","id":812198,"title":"HtR: Changing perceptions On The WoD","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-01-19T16:16:30-08:00","id":812198,"title":"HtR: Changing perceptions On The WoD","content":"Sorry for The typos.<br /> <br /> Im going to run a game of HtR, but i realized that my players know a bit too much about The WoD and its creatures, pol\u00edtics etc...<br /> <br /> Im trying to Do something to alter their perception, for them not to be able to guess what are They fighting or to which clan/tribe/tradici\u00f3n belongs. Advices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T16:53:04-08:00","id":812217,"title":"","content":"Hunter is actually the perfect thing for this. It doesn't really assume that the critters you encounter are the traditional monsters from WoD. Most of its supplements actually talk about using alternative and different monsters. So just take a look at those. Then feel free to mix it up with stuff like Wicked Dead for Requiem, the Hunter horror Recognition guide, Use Night's Black Agents from Pelgrane or the book of unremitting darkness. Open up old Ravenloft books. Heck, rewatch Buffy<br /> <br /> Go crazy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-19T17:02:54-08:00","id":812226,"title":"","content":"1) Communicate. Warn them to avoid preconceptions from other games. If they ignore that... well you can teach them fast.<br /> <br /> 2) As Asmodai said, HtR is awesome for this. You have a plethora of options for building your own monsters that don't follow the rules they're used to from other games. They can guess all they want, but a few times of &quot;Oh that must be a Brujah&quot; only to have such assumptions bite them in the ass is usually plenty for them to stop that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}